is problem  for many realistic budget distributions  finally we prove a robust hardness  result  that says no budget distribution  allows better than 90 approximation  because of the time limit i will not  show you the proof of any of these  results  but if you are interested you can read  the paper or send me an email  instead  i will show you the numeric simulation  for the second result  our numerical simulation computes  optimal approximation factors for  various budget distributions  by solving a non-convex program  on the left column you can see different  budget distributions we tried  there are some synthetic distributions  like uniform distribution log scale  uniform distributions  and there are also some real-world data  sets  like the top 10 ad campaign on facebook  ads  and the 2020 democratic  candidate campaigns  on the right column you can see the  worst case approximation ratios here  worst case stands for worst case module  function  and you can see non-negligible  improvement over the baseline one minus  one over e for all these distributions  in hindsight budget smooth analysis  alone is probably insufficient to  explain all the missing 37 percent  that said there's still some room to  improve  in comparison even the original north  most analysis showed a huge polynomial  runtime for the simplex algorithm but  now it is significantly improved  moreover here is why i believe  budget smooth analysis is important and  should be applied to other budget  constraint problems  budget smooth analysis provides  attractable beyond the worst case  performance test for the worst case  optimal algorithms of budget constraint  optimization problems  it helps us identify the right optimal  algorithm  by tractable i mean  the noise model of budget smooth  analysis  is reasonably simple  it allows us  to analytically solve for the best  algorithm  also  in practice we can easily  verify our assumption of budget  distribution  by calculating the empirical  distribution  let me give you a few examples  for the modular maximization we showed  that the worst case optimal greedy  algorithm is also optimal in the budget  smooth analysis model  so it passed the performance test  now i give you a negative example  so this is another recent project in  this direction  where we study procurement auction in  the large markets  so basically this is knapsack problem  so we have a buyer and a bunch of  sellers who have values and costs  the only difference is that in this  problem the costs are private  and therefore  we need to design a truthful auction for  the buyer  to give incentives to the sellers  and make them report the true costs  for procrimal auction problem  coincidentally the worst case optimal  choose for auction also has 1-1 over e  approximation  we prove that this auction is stuck at  1.1 over e for any budgeted distribution  it is not budget's most optimal so it  failed the performance test  instead we devised a new auction that is  budget's most optimal  and it passed the performance test  it beats 1-1 over e in expectation for  any non-trivial budget  by non-trivial i mean there has to be at  least two budgets in the support of the  distribution  that's not the end of the story  we further show that our new auction is  instantly optimal compared with a large  and natural class of auctions including  the previous or optimal auction  and empirically we saw that our auction  out performance  previous optimal auction by a large  margin  on realistic markets somebody from many  natural distributions  this slide shows the simulation results  of procurement auction on synthetic  markets  on the left column we have seller's  distribution of costs  so we use gaussian distribution uniform  distribution exponential distribution  and gaussian mixtures  on the right column we have the  approximation ratios of the previous  optimal auction and our auction  we can see that  the approximation ratio of previous  optimal auction is very close to 1-1  over e  for all the distributions  and our auction is able to outperform  the previous optimal auction by a large  margin  so the takeaway is if you designed a  worst case optimal algorithm for budget  constraint optimization problem  budget smooth analysis should  immediately be your next test  if your algorithm is budget's most  optimal this provides rigorous evidence  that your algorithm is probably also  good beyond the worst case  if not there might be better worst case  optimal algorithms that have better  performance in practice  and the budget smooth analysis could  serve as a heuristic that guides you  towards such algorithms  namely during your quest for the  budget's most optimal algorithm you  could find better worst case optimal  algorithm that performs better in  practice  this is exactly how we found the better  procurement auction  that's all i want to say  thanks for watching
 

